#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:12
msgid "Virtual machines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:14
msgid "VMs are run on the Linux Qemu/KVM hypervisor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:16
msgid "Virtual disks are stored in Ceph RBD volumes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:18
msgid ""
"The guest operating system is a 64-bit NixOS Linux managed by the Flying "
"Circus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:20
msgid ""
"Packages are installed through the managed components (roles) globally or"
" in your service user using Nix. You are also free to compile things in "
"your service users' home. However, on NixOS, this can have suprising "
"effects - talk to us if you need to do that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:24
msgid ""
"We are always looking for more components to manage for you but as a "
"general rule new managed components take their time to develop them. "
"Contact us if you would like to see a managed component we do not yet "
"support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:29
msgid ""
"CloudInit based operating systems are supported and managed by the "
"customer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:31
msgid "VMs can be assigned resources:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:33
msgid "1-12 virtual CPU cores"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:34
msgid ""
"1-128GiB RAM (the customer API limits you to 64GiB, talk to us if you "
"need more)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:35
msgid ""
"30GiB-10+TiB disk (note that filesystems become unwieldy at a certain "
"size, we strongly recommend looking into using our S3-compatible object "
"storage in those cases)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:37
msgid "Resources can be resized:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:39
msgid "CPU and RAM changes currently require a reboot of the VM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:40
msgid "Disks can be grown on the fly without a reboot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:41
msgid ""
"Shrinking disks is not supported. Growing a disk is very fast and thus we"
" recommend starting small and growing as needed. If you need to "
"drastically shrink a disk you need to provision a new VM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:45
msgid "Maintenance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:47
msgid ""
"For every project our automatic maintenance window is by default set "
"between 22:00 and 5:00 (Europe/Berlin) with a pre-announcement period of "
"12 hours."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:50
msgid ""
"When our tools notice that maintenance is required they will "
"automatically pick a window matching the configured limits and notify "
"your technical contacts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:53
msgid "Reboot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:55
msgid ""
"Automated reboots are announced according to the maintenance schedule. "
"Users granted the `sudo-srv` permission are able to reboot a VM "
"immediately via the customer portal at <https://my.flyingcircus.io>."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:58
msgid ""
"Machines should *not* be rebooted manually on the command line (e.g. "
"`sudo systemctl reboot`). Monitoring systems will consider this "
"*unplanned*, likely causing an alarm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:60
msgid "Deletion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:64
msgid ""
"VMs are deleted in a multi-stage process that takes around 38 days. You "
"can schedule the deletion of a VM at earliest for the next day (midnight "
"Europe/Berlin)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:68
msgid "The stages of deletion are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:70
msgid "Prepare"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:72
msgid "(t-5 days)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:74
msgid ""
"Create a maintenance period to let technical contacts know that a VM is "
"due for deletion soon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:77
msgid ""
"Also, add downtimes in our monitoring systems to stop any alerts related "
"to the VM starting from their deletion date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:80
msgid "Soft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:82
msgid "(at t=0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:84
msgid "Shutdown the VM but keep all existing records, IPs, disks, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:86
msgid ""
"At this point you can still cancel the deletion and start up the VM as it"
" was including all persistent data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:89
msgid "Hard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:91
msgid "(t+3 days)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:93
msgid "Delete the VMs hard disk from activate storage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:95
msgid "Also delete all records from our directory and allow the IPs to be reused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:97
msgid "Purge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:99
msgid "(t+32 days)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:101
msgid "Delete the VMs backups."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:103
msgid "Recycle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:105
msgid "(t+38 days)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:107
msgid ""
"Delete the VM deletion notice which will in turn allow the VMs name to be"
" used again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:111
msgid "Minimum memory requirements (NixOS-based VMS only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:113
msgid ""
"Even before your actual application starts, the operating system and its "
"infrastructure components require RAM. We have a minimum memory "
"requirement of 3 GiB for virtual VMs running our NixOS platform, which - "
"under extreme circumstances - be exhausted by system services."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:115
msgid ""
"To understand where our memory requirements come from and to check "
"whether we might be exceeding those assumptions, we provide a detailed "
"list of the expected memory consumption on a small machine. Some of those"
" usages are dynamic and may be (much) larger on larger VMs with a higher "
"load:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:117
msgid "Kernel internal structures (150 MiB)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:119
msgid ""
"On a 3 GiB VM the kernel reserves around 150 MiB for internal purposes in"
" a way  that this memory will not be visible in the \"MemTotal\" fields "
"of monitoring tools like \"top\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:122
#, python-format
msgid ""
"On larger machines this is expected to asymptotically reach around 2% of "
"the virtual memory the VM is provisioned with. A 64 GiB VM can thus "
"consume around 1,3 GiB of reserved kernel space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:124
msgid "System management tools (1.1 GiB)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:126
msgid ""
"Our platform is designed to provide reliable system upgrades and "
"deterministic states (\"predictable outcomes\"). To achieve this, we use "
"specialized agents—tools responsible for building the system and its "
"configuration while keeping it updated and clean. A large part of this "
"involves system configuration evaluation via nixos-rebuild, which runs "
"regularly (approximately every 10 minutes) to install new packages or "
"apply configuration changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:128
msgid ""
"I addition some jobs like preparing larger release upgrades or cleaning "
"the nix store may leverage a similar high amount. However, those tools "
"are prohibited from running in parallel, thus limiting the usage to a bit"
" more than 1 GiB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:130
msgid ""
"Some tools, like the nix store garbage collection, may use higher values "
"depending on the system usage profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:132
msgid "Monitoring and Telemetry (1 GiB)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:134
msgid ""
"We run a variety of tools to monitor systems for proper operations at all"
" times. Most tools are relatively light weight, but the number and "
"combination of application-specific tasks adds up, especially because "
"some of them spawn a number of (parallel) subprocesses to inspect the "
"system state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid "Component / Service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid "Reserved Memory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid "Function & Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid "**Telegraf**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid "256 MiB"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid ""
"**Metric Collection:** Continuously collects performance data (CPU, RAM, "
"Disk I/O) and sends it to our central dashboards for visualization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid "**Sensu**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid ""
"**Monitoring & Alerting:** Performs proactive system checks and reliably "
"triggers alarms in the event of failures or critical states."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid "**Alloy (optional)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid ""
"**Extended Telemetry:** A flexible agent for collecting, processing, and "
"forwarding metrics, logs, and traces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid "**Filebeat (1–2 instances)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid "100 MiB per instance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid ""
"**Log Shipper:** Collects local system and application logs and "
"transports them securely for platform-wide, central analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid "**systemd journal**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid "100 MiB"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid ""
"**Local Log Management:** Captures, stores, and structures the log output"
" of the kernel and all local services."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid "**Fail2ban**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:7
msgid ""
"**Intrusion Prevention:** Analyzes live logs and protects the server from"
" brute-force attacks by blocking IP addresses after repeated failed "
"logins (e.g., SSH)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:146
msgid "Baseline Linux userland (100 MiB)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:148
msgid ""
"This includes the SSH daemon, systemd, and a variety of userland "
"processes, including shells of logged-in users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:150
msgid "Target size for buffers and VFS cache (1 GiB)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:152
msgid ""
"For any system to stay responsive and operational hot data must be cached"
" in RAM and buffers must be available for data to stream from and to "
"devices and the network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:154
msgid "We expect around 1 GiB to be available for this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:156
msgid "Total Expected Memory Usage & Workloads (3 GiB Baseline)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:157
msgid ""
"When adding up the fixed and dynamic values mentioned above, it becomes "
"clear that a base system under load (e.g., during a system update while "
"monitoring is active) can easily consume 2 to 3 GB of RAM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:159
msgid ""
"The values provided here represent the observed maximums in healthy "
"systems. While these typically do not peak at exactly the same time, they"
" may do so during periods of high stress. We expect that, under normal "
"conditions, a VM with 3 GiB of RAM will be able to carry a small "
"application load (approx. 512 MiB) without frequent issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:161
msgid ""
"**What comes \"on top\"?** The actual workloads for which the server was "
"commissioned are added to this baseline consumption:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:164
msgid ""
"Component Roles: Databases like PostgreSQL or MySQL, Webgateway (NGINX, "
"HAProxy), Docker or container orchestration like K3s."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:166
msgid ""
"Frameworks & Applications: Your individual customer applications (e.g., "
"Ruby on Rails, Django, Node.js, Java)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:168
msgid "Swap handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:170
msgid ""
"To give systems some breathing room in unexpected situations we provide a"
" certain amount of swap on all machines so that the kernel can write some"
" data that is not currently needed on disk for a short period. To keep "
"systems as responsive as possible, we generally avoid placing data in "
"swap until significant memory pressure is detected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/infrastructure/vms/index.md:172
msgid ""
"If the memory pressure becomes too intense, the kernel will - at some "
"point - start killing processes. We manage this in a proactive way, so "
"that hard lockups are avoided and applications that are the likely "
"culprit of the high usage will be restarted while the system is still "
"healthy - avoiding unnecessary downtimes and giving direct feedback which"
" application caused the memory spike. Those are automatically tracked in "
"our ticket system and followed up on to investigate and adjust the system"
" parameters as needed - either optimizing the configuration or adjusting "
"the amount of available memory."
msgstr ""

